3.4.0

The development of EasyLocal++ 3 since 3.3 (Andrea Schaerf, Roberto Maria
Rosati, Francesca Da Ros, Luca Di Gaspero), merged from satt/easylocal-3.

Changes in behaviour:

* FirstDescent starts each scan from a random move
  (NeighborhoodExplorer::SelectRandomFirst), which compares moves with
  operator<; SelectFirst(start_move, ...) is gone.
* The random generator is faster and sized to the range drawn
  (utils/random.hh), so runs with the same seed take other trajectories than
  in 3.3.
* SimulatedAnnealing and SimulatedAnnealingEvaluationBased are one class,
  and the initial temperature, when not given, is estimated with a revised
  strategy.

Additions:

* SimulatedAnnealingOnlyCutoff: cools only once enough moves have been
  accepted (neighbors_accepted_ratio of a temperature's share of the
  evaluations).
* SimulatedAnnealingFixedTemperature, and SimulatedAnnealingWithReheating
  based on iterations.
* Tracing of the runners' events (include/tracing, docs/tracing.md) and
  logging; the current solution of a runner, not only the best.
* Revisions of Tabu Search and of the testers' menus; fixes of cut-off
  iterations, of max_neighbors_sampled across runs, of start_temperature and
  of the 16-bit random fallback.

3.3.1

* FirstDescent terminates: NeighborhoodExplorer::SelectFirst(start_move, ...)
  looped forever once the scan from start_move reached the last move without
  an acceptable move; it now explores cyclically, from the move after
  start_move to the last one, then from the first move back to start_move.

3.0 francis

* Code has been rewritten to meet C++11 standard
* Multi-threading support has changed accordingly to the previous point
* Code have been refactored to eliminate source of inefficiency

4.0 lucy

* Moved build system to CMake
* Now libraries get installed in system default paths